  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, I checked your account. It's active, it isn't locked, and it's waiting for you to set your own password, so your temporary password is still fine. The error usually means the new password doesn't meet our rules or the change is being done from the wrong place. Here's what to try:\n\n1. Change the password on your laptop's Windows sign-in screen, not on a web page. Before you start, make sure you're on the office network, or connected to VPN if you're at home.\n2. Type your temporary password carefully. Check that Caps Lock is off and your keyboard language is set correctly. Watch for characters that look alike, such as l and I, or 0 and O.\n3. Your new password must be at least 14 characters long and can't be a password you've used recently. A short phrase works well, for example several words with a number added.\n\nYour attempts so far haven't locked you out, so you can try again right away. If it still shows an error, please reply and tell us where you were signing in (Windows screen or a web page) and the exact error message. We'll take it from there and can issue a new temporary password if needed, which would be given to you by phone.",
  "internal_note": "Followed KB-003. lookup_user (id 12): account active, must_change_password=true, failed_login_count=0, not sign-in blocked, VPN access enabled. Password last set 2026-10-11 03:03 UTC (the onboarding temp password). Sign-in logs: 10 successful sign-ins from New York (corporate network and residential VPN), no failed password attempts, no anomalies. Note: none of the logged sign-ins show MFA, so check Duo enrollment as part of onboarding. Laptop BL-LT-0112 is online, checked in 2026-10-11 02:51 UTC, no warnings. No lockout, so no unlock needed. The most likely cause is the new password failing policy (at least 14 characters, no reuse) or the change being attempted on a web page or off-network. Gave the user KB-003 steps. If she reports it still fails on the Windows sign-in screen while on network/VPN, issue a new temp password per KB-002 (identity confirmed: request came from her own verified email) and deliver it by phone.",
